IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`
IMPORT `sgc2-common`
IMPORT `sgc2-s206-208a-duties`

-- Tests for sgc2-s206-208a-duties.l4 (sections 206, 207, 208 and 208A). Every expected value is written from the text of the sections, beside the assertion, not from the code.
-- Argument order is the order of the GIVEN lines of the function under test.

§ `Section 206(1): the notice that engages the company's duty`

-- Arguments: served, requires particulars of other emoluments, total members, members on whose behalf sent, total issued shares (excluding treasury), shares held by those on whose behalf sent.
-- (a) at least 5% of the members: 5 of 100 is exactly 5%; 4 of 100 is not.
#ASSERT `s 206(1) the notice engages the duty of the company` TRUE TRUE 100 5 1000 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 206(1) the notice engages the duty of the company` TRUE TRUE 100 4 1000 0 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (b) holders of not less than 5% of the issued shares (excluding treasury shares): 50 of 1,000, and 49 is not enough.
#ASSERT `s 206(1) the notice engages the duty of the company` TRUE TRUE 100 0 1000 50 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 206(1) the notice engages the duty of the company` TRUE TRUE 100 0 1000 49 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Both limbs met: still the same answer.
#ASSERT `s 206(1) the notice engages the duty of the company` TRUE TRUE 100 5 1000 50 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A notice sent on behalf of no one holds no percentage of anything.
#ASSERT `s 206(1) the notice engages the duty of the company` TRUE TRUE 0 0 0 0 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The notice must be served, and must require the particulars the subsection names.
#ASSERT `s 206(1) the notice engages the duty of the company` FALSE TRUE 100 5 1000 50 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 206(1) the notice engages the duty of the company` TRUE FALSE 100 5 1000 50 EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- (c), (d), (e): in default unless the act was done and done immediately; no default where the duty was not engaged.
#ASSERT `s 206(1)(c) the company is in default of the duty to prepare the statement` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 206(1)(c) the company is in default of the duty to prepare the statement` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 206(1)(c) the company is in default of the duty to prepare the statement` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 206(1)(c) the company is in default of the duty to prepare the statement` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 206(1)(d) the company is in default of the duty to forward a copy of the statement` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 206(1)(d) the company is in default of the duty to forward a copy of the statement` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 206(1)(d) the company is in default of the duty to forward a copy of the statement` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 206(1)(d) the company is in default of the duty to forward a copy of the statement` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 206(1)(e) the company is in default of the duty to lay the statement before the company in general meeting` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 206(1)(e) the company is in default of the duty to lay the statement before the company in general meeting` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 206(1)(e) the company is in default of the duty to lay the statement before the company in general meeting` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 206(1)(e) the company is in default of the duty to lay the statement before the company in general meeting` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- "immediately" has no number of days: the section's own standard of time sets the time, as the input `the period the standard of time allows, as found`, so each of these rules is fulfilled when done in time, ends BREACH when done late or not by then, and stays open until then.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 206(1)(c) the company must prepare the statement of the auditor's other emoluments` "Acme Pte Ltd" 7 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company "Acme Pte Ltd" DOES `s 206(1)(c) prepare a statement showing particulars of all emoluments paid to the auditor or other person and of the services in respect of which the payments have been made` AT 1

-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 206(1)(c) the company must prepare the statement of the auditor's other emoluments` "Acme Pte Ltd" 45 AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 400)

-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 206(1)(d) the company must forward a copy of the statement` "Acme Pte Ltd" 7 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company "Acme Pte Ltd" DOES `s 206(1)(d) forward a copy of the statement to all persons entitled to receive notice of general meetings of the company` AT 1

-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 206(1)(d) the company must forward a copy of the statement` "Acme Pte Ltd" 45 AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 400)

-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 206(1)(e) the company must lay the statement before the company in general meeting` "Acme Pte Ltd" 7 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company "Acme Pte Ltd" DOES `s 206(1)(e) lay the statement before the company in general meeting` AT 1

-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 206(1)(e) the company must lay the statement before the company in general meeting` "Acme Pte Ltd" 45 AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 400)

§ `Section 206(1A): the public company's review of the auditor's fees`

-- The circumstances are prescribed elsewhere: asked as a fact. A company that is not public, or circumstances not prescribed: the text does not say (NOTHING).
#ASSERT `s 206(1A) the duty of the public company to review the auditor's fees applies` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 206(1A) the duty of the public company to review the auditor's fees applies` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 206(1A) the duty of the public company to review the auditor's fees applies` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Duty applies: reviewed and sent is no default; reviewed but outcome not sent is a default; not reviewed is a default.
#ASSERT `s 206(1A) the company is in default of the duty to review the auditor's fees and send the outcome` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 206(1A) the company is in default of the duty to review the auditor's fees and send the outcome` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 206(1A) the company is in default of the duty to review the auditor's fees and send the outcome` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 206(1A) the company is in default of the duty to review the auditor's fees and send the outcome` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- The review comes first, then the outcome is sent: both done, fulfilled; only the first done, the second is still open; neither done, the first is still open.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 206(1A) the public company must review the auditor's fees and send the outcome` "Acme Pte Ltd" 7 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company "Acme Pte Ltd" DOES `s 206(1A) undertake a review of the fees, expenses and emoluments of the auditor to determine whether the independence of the auditor has been compromised` AT 1
    PARTY Company "Acme Pte Ltd" DOES `s 206(1A) send the outcome of the review to all persons entitled to receive notice of general meetings of the company` AT 2

-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 206(1A) the public company must review the auditor's fees and send the outcome` "Acme Pte Ltd" 45 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company "Acme Pte Ltd" DOES `s 206(1A) undertake a review of the fees, expenses and emoluments of the auditor to determine whether the independence of the auditor has been compromised` AT 1
    (WAITUNTIL 400)

-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 206(1A) the public company must review the auditor's fees and send the outcome` "Acme Pte Ltd" 7 AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 400)

§ `Section 206(2): the offence`

#ASSERT `s 206(2) the person is guilty of the offence` TRUE `s 205(17) the company` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 206(2) the person is guilty of the offence` TRUE `s 205(17) a director of the company who is in default` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 206(2) the person is guilty of the offence` TRUE `s 205(17) any other person` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 206(2) the person is guilty of the offence` FALSE `s 205(17) the company` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 206(2) the most the person may be fined on conviction` TRUE `s 205(17) the company` EQUALS JUST 5000
#ASSERT `s 206(2) the most the person may be fined on conviction` TRUE `s 205(17) a director of the company who is in default` EQUALS JUST 5000
#ASSERT `s 206(2) the most the person may be fined on conviction` TRUE `s 205(17) any other person` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 206(2) the most the person may be fined on conviction` FALSE `s 205(17) the company` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 207(1) and (1A)`

-- (1): reported on the financial statements and records; and, for a parent company with consolidated statements, on the consolidated statements too.
#ASSERT `s 207(1) the auditor is in default of the duty to report to the members` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 207(1) the auditor is in default of the duty to report to the members` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 207(1) the auditor is in default of the duty to report to the members` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 207(1) the auditor is in default of the duty to report to the members` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 207(1) the auditor is in default of the duty to report to the members` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- The report to the members: (1) gives it no time of its own, but (1A) says "in sufficient time" of a report under (1), so the section's own standard of time is the input `the period the standard of time allows, as found`: 45 days in both traces, the report on day 10 in time and a wait to day 400 past it.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 207(1) the auditor must report to the members` "Lim & Co" 45 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Auditor "Lim & Co" DOES `s 207(1) report to the members` AT 10

-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 207(1) the auditor must report to the members` "Lim & Co" 45 AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 400)

-- (1A): furnished in sufficient time.
#ASSERT `s 207(1A) the auditor is in default of the duty to furnish the report to the directors in sufficient time` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 207(1A) the auditor is in default of the duty to furnish the report to the directors in sufficient time` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 207(1A) the auditor is in default of the duty to furnish the report to the directors in sufficient time` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "no offence is committed by an auditor under this subsection if the directors have not submitted the financial statements for audit ... in sufficient time".
#ASSERT `s 207(1A) the auditor commits no offence under the subsection` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The directors did submit in time: the text does not say whether an offence is committed.
#ASSERT `s 207(1A) the auditor commits no offence under the subsection` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 207(1A) the auditor must furnish the report to the directors in sufficient time` "Lim & Co" 45 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Auditor "Lim & Co" DOES `s 207(1A) furnish the report to the directors in sufficient time` AT 10

-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 207(1A) the auditor must furnish the report to the directors in sufficient time` "Lim & Co" 7 AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 400)

§ `Section 207(2): what the report must state`

-- (a): arguments: states compliance, states true and fair (company), parent company with consolidated statements, states compliance (consolidated), states true and fair (group).
#ASSERT `s 207(2)(a) the auditor is in default of the duty to state the opinions on the financial statements` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 207(2)(a) the auditor is in default of the duty to state the opinions on the financial statements` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 207(2)(a) the auditor is in default of the duty to state the opinions on the financial statements` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A parent company with consolidated statements: the opinions on those are required too.
#ASSERT `s 207(2)(a) the auditor is in default of the duty to state the opinions on the financial statements` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 207(2)(a) the auditor is in default of the duty to state the opinions on the financial statements` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 207(2)(a) the auditor is in default of the duty to state the opinions on the financial statements` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (aa): non-compliance not approved by the Registrar and not allowed by the Minister's order: the report must say whether it is necessary for a true and fair view.
#ASSERT `s 207(2)(aa) the auditor is in default of the duty to state whether the non-compliance is necessary for a true and fair view` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 207(2)(aa) the auditor is in default of the duty to state whether the non-compliance is necessary for a true and fair view` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 207(2)(aa) the auditor is in default of the duty to state whether the non-compliance is necessary for a true and fair view` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 207(2)(aa) the auditor is in default of the duty to state whether the non-compliance is necessary for a true and fair view` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 207(2)(aa) the auditor is in default of the duty to state whether the non-compliance is necessary for a true and fair view` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (b), (d), (e).
#ASSERT `s 207(2)(b) the auditor is in default of the duty to state whether the records have been properly kept` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 207(2)(b) the auditor is in default of the duty to state whether the records have been properly kept` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 207(2)(d) the auditor is in default of the duty to state the defect, irregularity or matter` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 207(2)(d) the auditor is in default of the duty to state the defect, irregularity or matter` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 207(2)(d) the auditor is in default of the duty to state the defect, irregularity or matter` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 207(2)(e) the auditor is in default of the duty to state the reasons for not being satisfied` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 207(2)(e) the auditor is in default of the duty to state the reasons for not being satisfied` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 207(2)(e) the auditor is in default of the duty to state the reasons for not being satisfied` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Section 207(3) and (4)`

-- (3): arguments: opinion on (a), (b), (c), consolidated statements prepared otherwise than as one set, opinion on (e).
#ASSERT `s 207(3) the auditor is in default of the duty to form an opinion on each of the matters` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 207(3) the auditor is in default of the duty to form an opinion on each of the matters` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 207(3) the auditor is in default of the duty to form an opinion on each of the matters` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 207(3) the auditor is in default of the duty to form an opinion on each of the matters` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (e) is a matter only where consolidated statements are prepared otherwise than as one set.
#ASSERT `s 207(3) the auditor is in default of the duty to form an opinion on each of the matters` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 207(3) the auditor is in default of the duty to form an opinion on each of the matters` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 207(3) the auditor is in default of the duty to state particulars of a deficiency, failure or shortcoming` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 207(3) the auditor is in default of the duty to state particulars of a deficiency, failure or shortcoming` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 207(3) the auditor is in default of the duty to state particulars of a deficiency, failure or shortcoming` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (4): a subsidiary corporation not incorporated in Singapore, of a Singapore parent company: no opinion is required. Elsewhere the text is silent.
#ASSERT `s 207(4) the auditor is not required to form an opinion on whether the records of the subsidiary corporation have been kept in accordance with this Act` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 207(4) the auditor is not required to form an opinion on whether the records of the subsidiary corporation have been kept in accordance with this Act` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 207(4) the auditor is not required to form an opinion on whether the records of the subsidiary corporation have been kept in accordance with this Act` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 207(5), (6) and (11)`

-- (11): only a register kept under Part 11A is taken out.
#ASSERT `s 207(11) the item is excluded from the reference to registers in subsections (5), (6) and (10)` `s 207(5) a register kept under Part 11A` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 207(11) the item is excluded from the reference to registers in subsections (5), (6) and (10)` `s 207(5) a register other than a register kept under Part 11A` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 207(11) the item is excluded from the reference to registers in subsections (5), (6) and (10)` `s 207(5) an accounting or other record that is not a register` EQUALS NOTHING
-- (5): the auditor of the company has a right of access to accounting and other records, including registers, but not a Part 11A register.
#ASSERT `s 207(5) the auditor has a right of access at all times to the item` TRUE `s 207(5) an accounting or other record that is not a register` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 207(5) the auditor has a right of access at all times to the item` TRUE `s 207(5) a register other than a register kept under Part 11A` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 207(5) the auditor has a right of access at all times to the item` TRUE `s 207(5) a register kept under Part 11A` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not an auditor of the company: the subsection is silent.
#ASSERT `s 207(5) the auditor has a right of access at all times to the item` FALSE `s 207(5) an accounting or other record that is not a register` EQUALS NOTHING
-- (5), the right to require: arguments: asker is auditor of the company, person asked, the three limbs of section 6 for the other company, information the auditor desires for the audit.
#ASSERT `s 207(5) the auditor is entitled to require information and explanations from the person` TRUE `s 207(5) an officer of the company` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- An auditor of a company deemed related by section 6: each limb of section 6 on its own.
#ASSERT `s 207(5) the auditor is entitled to require information and explanations from the person` TRUE `s 207(5) an auditor of another company` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 207(5) the auditor is entitled to require information and explanations from the person` TRUE `s 207(5) an auditor of another company` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 207(5) the auditor is entitled to require information and explanations from the person` TRUE `s 207(5) an auditor of another company` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not related by section 6: the text says nothing of that auditor.
#ASSERT `s 207(5) the auditor is entitled to require information and explanations from the person` TRUE `s 207(5) an auditor of another company` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 207(5) the auditor is entitled to require information and explanations from the person` TRUE `s 207(5) any other person` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- What the auditor does not desire for the purposes of audit; and a person who is not the auditor.
#ASSERT `s 207(5) the auditor is entitled to require information and explanations from the person` TRUE `s 207(5) an officer of the company` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 207(5) the auditor is entitled to require information and explanations from the person` FALSE `s 207(5) an officer of the company` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (6): the auditor of a parent company for which consolidated statements are required, as to a subsidiary corporation.
#ASSERT `s 207(6) the auditor has a right of access at all times to the item of the subsidiary corporation` TRUE `s 207(5) an accounting or other record that is not a register` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 207(6) the auditor has a right of access at all times to the item of the subsidiary corporation` TRUE `s 207(5) a register other than a register kept under Part 11A` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 207(6) the auditor has a right of access at all times to the item of the subsidiary corporation` TRUE `s 207(5) a register kept under Part 11A` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 207(6) the auditor has a right of access at all times to the item of the subsidiary corporation` FALSE `s 207(5) an accounting or other record that is not a register` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 207(6) the auditor is entitled, at the expense of the parent company, to require information and explanations from the person` TRUE `s 207(6) an officer of a subsidiary corporation` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 207(6) the auditor is entitled, at the expense of the parent company, to require information and explanations from the person` TRUE `s 207(6) an auditor of a subsidiary corporation` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 207(6) the auditor is entitled, at the expense of the parent company, to require information and explanations from the person` TRUE `s 207(6) any other person` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 207(6) the auditor is entitled, at the expense of the parent company, to require information and explanations from the person` TRUE `s 207(6) an officer of a subsidiary corporation` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 207(6) the auditor is entitled, at the expense of the parent company, to require information and explanations from the person` FALSE `s 207(6) an officer of a subsidiary corporation` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 207(7) and (8)`

-- (7): arguments: attached or endorsed, a member required it read, it has been read, open to inspection.
#ASSERT `s 207(7) the report is attached or endorsed, read on a member's request and open to inspection as the subsection requires` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A member required it read: it must have been read.
#ASSERT `s 207(7) the report is attached or endorsed, read on a member's request and open to inspection as the subsection requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 207(7) the report is attached or endorsed, read on a member's request and open to inspection as the subsection requires` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 207(7) the report is attached or endorsed, read on a member's request and open to inspection as the subsection requires` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 207(7) the report is attached or endorsed, read on a member's request and open to inspection as the subsection requires` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (8): the auditor, or the agent authorised in writing; no one else.
#ASSERT `s 207(8) the person is entitled to attend any general meeting of the company` `s 207(8) an auditor of the company` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 207(8) the person is entitled to attend any general meeting of the company` `s 207(8) an agent authorised by the auditor in writing for the purpose` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 207(8) the person is entitled to attend any general meeting of the company` `s 207(8) any other person` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 207(8) the person is entitled to receive all notices of, and other communications relating to, any general meeting which a member is entitled to receive` `s 207(8) an auditor of the company` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 207(8) the person is entitled to receive all notices of, and other communications relating to, any general meeting which a member is entitled to receive` `s 207(8) an agent authorised by the auditor in writing for the purpose` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 207(8) the person is entitled to receive all notices of, and other communications relating to, any general meeting which a member is entitled to receive` `s 207(8) any other person` EQUALS NOTHING
-- To be heard: at a meeting the person attends, on business that concerns the auditor as auditor.
#ASSERT `s 207(8) the person is entitled to be heard at the general meeting on the part of the business` `s 207(8) an auditor of the company` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 207(8) the person is entitled to be heard at the general meeting on the part of the business` `s 207(8) an agent authorised by the auditor in writing for the purpose` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 207(8) the person is entitled to be heard at the general meeting on the part of the business` `s 207(8) an auditor of the company` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 207(8) the person is entitled to be heard at the general meeting on the part of the business` `s 207(8) an auditor of the company` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 207(8) the person is entitled to be heard at the general meeting on the part of the business` `s 207(8) any other person` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 207(9) to (9D)`

-- (9): a breach the auditor is satisfied of, not adequately dealt with in the report or by telling the directors, to be reported at once to the Registrar.
#ASSERT `s 207(9) the auditor is in default of the duty to report the matter to the Registrar` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 207(9) the auditor is in default of the duty to report the matter to the Registrar` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Reported, but not immediately.
#ASSERT `s 207(9) the auditor is in default of the duty to report the matter to the Registrar` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Either limb of the "if" not met: no duty.
#ASSERT `s 207(9) the auditor is in default of the duty to report the matter to the Registrar` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 207(9) the auditor is in default of the duty to report the matter to the Registrar` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 207(9) the auditor must report the matter in writing to the Registrar` "Lim & Co" 45 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Auditor "Lim & Co" DOES `s 207(9) report the matter in writing to the Registrar` AT 1

-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 207(9) the auditor must report the matter in writing to the Registrar` "Lim & Co" 7 AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 400)

-- (9D): imprisonment for a term not less than 2 years and property not less than $100,000, both limbs, on both sides of each threshold.
#ASSERT `s 207(9D) the offence is a serious offence involving fraud or dishonesty` 2 100000 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 207(9D) the offence is a serious offence involving fraud or dishonesty` 10 5000000 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 207(9D) the offence is a serious offence involving fraud or dishonesty` 1.99 100000 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 207(9D) the offence is a serious offence involving fraud or dishonesty` 2 99999 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 207(9D) the offence is a serious offence involving fraud or dishonesty` 1 50000 EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- (9C): the auditor under a duty to report to the Monetary Authority of Singapore who already has.
#ASSERT `s 207(9C) the auditor is not required to make a report to the Minister under subsection (9A)` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Under the duty but not yet reported to the Authority: the text does not relieve the auditor.
#ASSERT `s 207(9C) the auditor is not required to make a report to the Minister under subsection (9A)` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 207(9C) the auditor is not required to make a report to the Minister under subsection (9A)` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- (9A): arguments: auditor of a public company or its subsidiary corporation, reason to believe, years, value, relieved by (9C), reported to the Minister, immediately.
#ASSERT `s 207(9A) the auditor is in default of the duty to report the matter to the Minister` TRUE TRUE 2 100000 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 207(9A) the auditor is in default of the duty to report the matter to the Minister` TRUE TRUE 2 100000 FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 207(9A) the auditor is in default of the duty to report the matter to the Minister` TRUE TRUE 2 100000 FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Below either threshold of (9D): not a serious offence in the sense of (9A).
#ASSERT `s 207(9A) the auditor is in default of the duty to report the matter to the Minister` TRUE TRUE 1.99 100000 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 207(9A) the auditor is in default of the duty to report the matter to the Minister` TRUE TRUE 2 99999 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Relieved by (9C); not the auditor of a public company or its subsidiary corporation; no reason to believe.
#ASSERT `s 207(9A) the auditor is in default of the duty to report the matter to the Minister` TRUE TRUE 2 100000 TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 207(9A) the auditor is in default of the duty to report the matter to the Minister` FALSE TRUE 2 100000 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 207(9A) the auditor is in default of the duty to report the matter to the Minister` TRUE FALSE 2 100000 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 207(9A) the auditor must report the matter to the Minister` "Lim & Co" 45 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Auditor "Lim & Co" DOES `s 207(9A) report the matter to the Minister` AT 1

-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 207(9A) the auditor must report the matter to the Minister` "Lim & Co" 7 AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 400)

-- (9B): a report to the Minister in good faith contravenes no duty; otherwise the text is silent.
#ASSERT `s 207(9B) no duty to which the auditor is subject is regarded as contravened by the report` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 207(9B) no duty to which the auditor is subject is regarded as contravened by the report` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 207(9B) no duty to which the auditor is subject is regarded as contravened by the report` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 207(10)`

-- Arguments: the person, the conduct, lawful excuse, the item refused (read through subsection (11)).
-- (a): an officer of a company who refuses or fails, without lawful excuse, to allow the company's auditor access.
#ASSERT `s 207(10) the person is guilty of the offence` `s 207(10) an officer of a company` `s 207(10)(a) refused or failed to allow an auditor of the company access in accordance with subsection (5)` FALSE `s 207(5) an accounting or other record that is not a register` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 207(10) the person is guilty of the offence` `s 207(10) an officer of a company` `s 207(10)(a) refused or failed to allow an auditor of the company access in accordance with subsection (5)` FALSE `s 207(5) a register other than a register kept under Part 11A` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- With lawful excuse: an element of the offence is missing.
#ASSERT `s 207(10) the person is guilty of the offence` `s 207(10) an officer of a company` `s 207(10)(a) refused or failed to allow an auditor of the company access in accordance with subsection (5)` TRUE `s 207(5) an accounting or other record that is not a register` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A register kept under Part 11A is not within subsection (5).
#ASSERT `s 207(10) the person is guilty of the offence` `s 207(10) an officer of a company` `s 207(10)(a) refused or failed to allow an auditor of the company access in accordance with subsection (5)` FALSE `s 207(5) a register kept under Part 11A` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not an officer of a company (paragraph (a) names no one else).
#ASSERT `s 207(10) the person is guilty of the offence` `s 207(10) an officer of a subsidiary corporation` `s 207(10)(a) refused or failed to allow an auditor of the company access in accordance with subsection (5)` FALSE `s 207(5) an accounting or other record that is not a register` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 207(10) the person is guilty of the offence` `s 207(10) any other person` `s 207(10)(a) refused or failed to allow an auditor of the company access in accordance with subsection (5)` FALSE `s 207(5) an accounting or other record that is not a register` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (b): an officer or auditor of a subsidiary corporation refusing the parent company's auditor.
#ASSERT `s 207(10) the person is guilty of the offence` `s 207(10) an officer of a subsidiary corporation` `s 207(10)(b) refused or failed to allow an auditor of the parent company access in accordance with subsection (6)` FALSE `s 207(5) an accounting or other record that is not a register` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 207(10) the person is guilty of the offence` `s 207(10) an auditor of a subsidiary corporation` `s 207(10)(b) refused or failed to allow an auditor of the parent company access in accordance with subsection (6)` FALSE `s 207(5) an accounting or other record that is not a register` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 207(10) the person is guilty of the offence` `s 207(10) an officer of a company` `s 207(10)(b) refused or failed to allow an auditor of the parent company access in accordance with subsection (6)` FALSE `s 207(5) an accounting or other record that is not a register` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 207(10) the person is guilty of the offence` `s 207(10) an officer of a subsidiary corporation` `s 207(10)(b) refused or failed to allow an auditor of the parent company access in accordance with subsection (6)` TRUE `s 207(5) an accounting or other record that is not a register` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 207(10) the person is guilty of the offence` `s 207(10) an officer of a subsidiary corporation` `s 207(10)(b) refused or failed to allow an auditor of the parent company access in accordance with subsection (6)` FALSE `s 207(5) a register kept under Part 11A` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (c): refusing or failing to give information or explanation as and when required: an officer of a company, or an officer or auditor of a subsidiary corporation.
#ASSERT `s 207(10) the person is guilty of the offence` `s 207(10) an officer of a company` `s 207(10)(c) refused or failed to give information or explanation as and when required under subsection (5) or (6)` FALSE `s 207(5) an accounting or other record that is not a register` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 207(10) the person is guilty of the offence` `s 207(10) an officer of a subsidiary corporation` `s 207(10)(c) refused or failed to give information or explanation as and when required under subsection (5) or (6)` FALSE `s 207(5) an accounting or other record that is not a register` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 207(10) the person is guilty of the offence` `s 207(10) an auditor of a subsidiary corporation` `s 207(10)(c) refused or failed to give information or explanation as and when required under subsection (5) or (6)` FALSE `s 207(5) an accounting or other record that is not a register` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 207(10) the person is guilty of the offence` `s 207(10) any other person` `s 207(10)(c) refused or failed to give information or explanation as and when required under subsection (5) or (6)` FALSE `s 207(5) an accounting or other record that is not a register` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 207(10) the person is guilty of the offence` `s 207(10) an officer of a company` `s 207(10)(c) refused or failed to give information or explanation as and when required under subsection (5) or (6)` TRUE `s 207(5) an accounting or other record that is not a register` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (c) concerns information, not access: a Part 11A register in the item makes no difference.
#ASSERT `s 207(10) the person is guilty of the offence` `s 207(10) an officer of a company` `s 207(10)(c) refused or failed to give information or explanation as and when required under subsection (5) or (6)` FALSE `s 207(5) a register kept under Part 11A` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (d): hindering, obstructing or delaying: no "without lawful excuse" in the paragraph, so an excuse changes nothing.
#ASSERT `s 207(10) the person is guilty of the offence` `s 207(10) an officer of a company` `s 207(10)(d) otherwise hindered, obstructed or delayed an auditor in the performance of the auditor's duties or the exercise of the auditor's powers under section 207` FALSE `s 207(5) an accounting or other record that is not a register` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 207(10) the person is guilty of the offence` `s 207(10) an auditor of a subsidiary corporation` `s 207(10)(d) otherwise hindered, obstructed or delayed an auditor in the performance of the auditor's duties or the exercise of the auditor's powers under section 207` TRUE `s 207(5) an accounting or other record that is not a register` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 207(10) the person is guilty of the offence` `s 207(10) any other person` `s 207(10)(d) otherwise hindered, obstructed or delayed an auditor in the performance of the auditor's duties or the exercise of the auditor's powers under section 207` FALSE `s 207(5) an accounting or other record that is not a register` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The fine: not exceeding $4,000 for the persons made guilty.
#ASSERT `s 207(10) the most the person may be fined on conviction` `s 207(10) an officer of a company` `s 207(10)(a) refused or failed to allow an auditor of the company access in accordance with subsection (5)` FALSE `s 207(5) an accounting or other record that is not a register` EQUALS JUST 4000
#ASSERT `s 207(10) the most the person may be fined on conviction` `s 207(10) any other person` `s 207(10)(a) refused or failed to allow an auditor of the company access in accordance with subsection (5)` FALSE `s 207(5) an accounting or other record that is not a register` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 208`

-- (1): a statement made in the course of the auditor's duties, no malice: not liable. With malice, the text does not say.
#ASSERT `s 208(1) the auditor is not liable to an action for defamation in respect of the statement` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 208(1) the auditor is not liable to an action for defamation in respect of the statement` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 208(1) the auditor is not liable to an action for defamation in respect of the statement` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2): the publication of a document an auditor prepared in the course of duty and that this Act requires to be lodged with the Registrar.
#ASSERT `s 208(2) the person is not liable to an action for defamation in respect of the publication of the document` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 208(2) the person is not liable to an action for defamation in respect of the publication of the document` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 208(2) the person is not liable to an action for defamation in respect of the publication of the document` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (3): the section does not limit another right, privilege or immunity as defendant in an action for defamation.
#ASSERT `s 208(3) section 208 limits or affects the right, privilege or immunity` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 208(3) section 208 limits or affects the right, privilege or immunity` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 208A`

-- (1): arguments: the provision exempts or indemnifies, a liability that by law would otherwise attach, in respect of negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust.
#ASSERT `s 208A(1) the provision is void` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 208A(1) the provision is void` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 208A(1) the provision is void` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 208A(1) the provision is void` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2): arguments: defending proceedings, judgment in favour or acquittal, connection with an application, relief granted.
#ASSERT `s 208A(2) the section does not prevent the company from indemnifying the auditor` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 208A(2) the section does not prevent the company from indemnifying the auditor` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Defending proceedings that did not end in the auditor's favour: not within (a).
#ASSERT `s 208A(2) the section does not prevent the company from indemnifying the auditor` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- An application under section 76A(13) or 391, relief refused: not within (b).
#ASSERT `s 208A(2) the section does not prevent the company from indemnifying the auditor` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Together: what (2) lets through is not void; what it does not, takes the answer of (1).
#ASSERT `s 208A(1) and (2) the provision is void under the section` TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 208A(1) and (2) the provision is void under the section` FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 208A(1) and (2) the provision is void under the section` FALSE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
